      "quote": "Using all the data to perform feature selection results in an accuracy score much higher than chance, even though our targets are completely random."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "sha256:b9c5023d2c98d714e341cacd0b3b1d7256049d72a93cc231e2bc600db983b500",
      "quote": "The train dataset is scaled, but not the test dataset, so model performance on the test dataset is worse than expected"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "sha256:b9c5023d2c98d714e341cacd0b3b1d7256049d72a93cc231e2bc600db983b500",
      "quote": "Alternatively, we recommend using a Pipeline , which makes it easier to chain transformations with estimators, and reduces the possibility of forgetting a transformation"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "answer",
  "answer": "The mismatch occurs because the training data is scaled while the test data is not transformed. A fitted Pipeline ensures that the same transformations applied during training are applied to the test data, preventing data leakage and ensuring consistent feature scaling.",
